op. A one-stop flight for $199 was cheaper, but I skipped it because you asked for nonstop.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge, New York. Check-in is 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, so $378 total. It was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Trip total:** $667, charged to the corporate card. That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\nThe flight and hotel ended up as two separate bookings, not one combined booking. The combined booking request timed out, but the flight still got booked and the hotel didn't. Retrying the combined booking could have charged for the flight twice, so I booked the hotel on its own.", "type": "text"}]}]}